<p><b>This is not a replacement for the <a href="https://github.com/desertwitch/par2cron#readme" target="_blank">full documentation (on GitHub)</a>.</b><br>
It is a condensed guide meant to get you started and as a cheatsheet.</p>

<h2>Getting started:</h2>
<p>Place a <code>_par2cron</code> marker file in any folder you want protected.<br>
par2cron will create parity data, periodically verify integrity, and repair corruption.</p>
<p><b>par2cron is suitable mostly only for non-changing content (such as media/backups).</b></p>

<h2>Protecting a folder:</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Navigate to a folder containing files you want to protect</li>
  <li>Create an empty "marker" file named <code>_par2cron</code></li>
  <li>Done - a PAR2 set is created on the next scheduled run!</li>
</ol>

<p>After creation of the PAR2 set, the marker file is normally deleted automatically.</p>
<p>PAR2 sets are then periodically verified and repaired with according to the schedule.</p>

<pre>Pictures/
|-- Nature/
|-- _par2cron  <-- par2cron marker file
|-- beach.jpg  <-- will be protected using PAR2
+-- sunset.jpg <-- will be protected using PAR2</pre>

<div style="display: inline-block; margin: 15px 0; border: 1px solid; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; opacity: 0.9;">
  <div style="padding: 4px 12px; font-weight: bold; font-size: 0.9em; border-bottom: 1px solid;">
    MENTAL MODEL: ONE PAR2 PER FOLDER
  </div>
  <div style="padding: 10px 12px; font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.4;">
    For more predictable protection, subfolders <u>are not</u> recursed into by default.
    <br>The flat scope ensures you always know exactly which files a PAR2 set covers.
    <div style="margin-top: 5px; font-style: italic; font-size: 0.9em;">
      For subfolder protection, choose between <a href="https://github.com/desertwitch/par2cron#deep-patterns-containing--or-" target="_blank">deep glob patterns</a> and <a href="https://github.com/desertwitch/par2cron#recursive-mode" target="_blank">recursive mode</a>.
      <br>Be advised that these modes are best set on a per-job basis via marker configuration.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Marker filename modifiers (optional):</h2>
<p>Append <code>par2</code> <a href="https://github.com/Parchive/par2cmdline#using-par2cmdline" target="_blank"><b>arguments</b></a> to the marker filename to influence creation defaults (for that folder):</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Marker file name</th><th>Resulting arguments (assuming defaults: <code>-r15 -n1</code>)</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>_par2cron</code></td><td>Uses defaults: <code>-r15 -n1</code></td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>_par2cron_r30</code></td><td>30% redundancy: <code>-r30 -n1</code></td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>_par2cron_q</code></td><td>Quiet mode added: <code>-r15 -n1 -q</code></td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>_par2cron_r30_q</code></td><td>Both above changes: <code>-r30 -n1 -q</code></td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>_par2cron_R</code></td><td>Recursive mode added: <code>-r15 -n1 -R</code></td></tr>
</table>
<p>Hint: <code>_R</code> in a marker filename forces recursive mode even without (below) YAML <code>mode</code> directive.</p>

<h2>Marker content modifiers (optional):</h2>
<p>For more defaults override control, you can put YAML directives inside the marker file:</p>
<pre>name: "Ubuntu"        # PAR2 set name (folder mode only)
args: ["-r30", "-n1"] # Replaces default par2 arguments
glob: "*.iso"         # Protect only the matching files
mode: "folder"        # "folder", "nested", "file" or "recursive"
verify: true          # Verify PAR2 set as part of creation
hidden: true          # Create PAR2 set as hidden (dotfiles)
persist: true         # Do not delete marker file after creation
bundle: true          # Create only one file (embed manifest in PAR2)
</pre>
<p>All directives are optional - only specify what you need to override.</p>
<p>Refer to <a href="https://github.com/desertwitch/par2cron?tab=readme-ov-file#creation-glob-patterns" target="_blank">"Creation Glob Patterns"</a> in documentation for supported glob patterns.</p>
<p>Beware that this applies only for the individual creation job (the folder with the marker file).</p>

<h2>Creation modes:</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>folder</strong> (default): One PAR2 set for all matching files</li>
  <li><strong>nested</strong>: One PAR2 set per folder containing matching files</li>
  <li><strong>file</strong>: One PAR2 set per matching file</li>
  <li><strong>recursive</strong>: One PAR2 set, using <code>par2</code>'s own internal recursion</li>
</ul>
<p>Refer to <a href="https://github.com/desertwitch/par2cron?tab=readme-ov-file#creation-modes" target="_blank">"Creation Modes"</a> in documentation for more in-depth explanations.</p>

<h2>Ignoring folders:</h2>
<ul>
  <li><code>.par2cron-ignore</code> - skip this folder</li>
  <li><code>.par2cron-ignore-all</code> - skip this folder and all subfolders</li>
</ul>
<p>A present ignore-file excludes the folder from all par2cron commands.</p>

<h2>Re-creating a PAR2 set:</h2>
<p>If you added/changed/removed protected files:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Delete existing PAR2-related files (see below)</li>
  <li>Create again a marker file named <code>_par2cron</code></li>
  <li>Done - a new PAR2 set is created on the next scheduled run!</li>
</ol>
<p>Second step does not apply when marker file was set to <code>persist</code>.</p>

<h2>Explanation of the generated files:</h2>
<pre>Pictures/
|-- beach.jpg
|-- sunset.jpg
|-- Pictures.par2           # PAR2 index file
|-- Pictures.vol00+01.par2  # PAR2 recovery data
|-- Pictures.par2.json      # par2cron manifest
+-- Pictures.par2.lock      # par2cron lockfile</pre>

<p>If the amount of files bothers you, you should use <a href="https://github.com/desertwitch/par2cron?tab=readme-ov-file#creation-as-bundle" target="_blank">bundle creation</a> instead.</p>
<p>Alternatively, you can switch on <code>hidden</code> creation to hide these files from view.</p>

